# The raw dataset passed GitHub's 100MB file limit (100.84MB) and is byte-identical
# to its own gzip, so only the ~14MB .gz copy is committed. Readers go through
# proofmatch/dataset_io.py, which falls back to the .gz when the .jsonl is absent.
dataset/tcslib_theorems.jsonl

# --- policy-cleanup working area (process artifacts, not library content) ---
# scripts/{decl_snapshot,decl_snapshot_diff,policy_build,style_lint,code_diff}.py write here:
# the plan, per-file audits, verification reports, per-declaration snapshots (~18 MB),
# scratch oleans and the lean lock. Regenerable; not part of the library.
# To keep the audit trail in the repo instead, un-ignore the small text parts:
#   !cleanup/PLAN.md
#   !cleanup/plans/
#   !cleanup/reports/
cleanup/

# Generated next to its input by the have->lemma metaprogram fixtures in TCSlib/Tactics
# (see HANDOFF.md). Regenerate with the fixture; never commit.
*_iter_output.lean
*.lean.progress
